#: ../../webgis-src/chc1_geoserver-introduction/sec01_introduction/section.rst:4
msgid "Introduction to GeoServer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc1_geoserver-introduction/sec01_introduction/section.rst:6
msgid ""
"GeoServer is a J2EE implementation of OpenGIS web server specification. "
"GeoServer can easily publish map data and allow users to update, delete "
"and insert feature data. GeoServer can easily and quickly share spatial "
"geographic information among users. GeoServer is a community open source "
"project, which can be downloaded directly through the community website. "
"Please refer to the resource table at the end of this document for "
"details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc1_geoserver-introduction/sec01_introduction/section.rst:14
msgid ""
"GeoServer is a J2EE implementation of OpenGIS web server specification. "
"GeoServer can easily publish map data and allow users to update, delete "
"and insert feature data. GeoServer can easily and quickly share spatial "
"geographic information among users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc1_geoserver-introduction/sec01_introduction/section.rst:20
msgid "Main features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc1_geoserver-introduction/sec01_introduction/section.rst:22
msgid ""
"Compatible with WMS and WFS features; support PostgreSQL, Shapefile, "
"ArcSDE, Oracle, VPF, MySQL, MapInfo; support hundreds of projections; can"
" output network map to jpeg, gif, png, SVG, KML and other formats; can "
"run on any J2EE/Servlet-based container; embed MapBuilder support AJAX "
"map client OpenLayers;, in addition to many other features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc1_geoserver-introduction/sec02_setup/section.rst:4
msgid "Install and configure GeoServer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc1_geoserver-introduction/sec02_setup/section.rst:6
msgid ""
"GeoServer is an open source server for sharing geospatial data. GeoServer"
" implements industry standard OGC protocols such as Web Feature Service "
"(WFS), Web Map Service (WMS), and Web Coverage Service (WCS). Additional "
"formats and publishing options are available as extensions, including Web"
" Processing Service (WPS) and Web Map Tile Service (WMTS). Both can be "
"published using GeoServer as a server. Before using the GeoServer server,"
" you need to download and install another web server tomcat. Someone may "
"have already installed it, but it needs to be configured."
msgstr ""

